    <testcase name="ehr/create_twice row 1" classname="ehr/create_twice">
      <failure message="step create-again: expected status 409, received status 201" type="server">FAILED   ehr/create_twice   step create-again
What     Create an EHR with the same ehr_id again.
Why      specs/openehr/ITS-REST/specifications/responses/409_EHR_with_id.yaml, description:
         &quot;Can happen when the supplied `ehr_id` is already used by an existing EHR.&quot;
         https://example.org/409_EHR_with_id.yaml
Expected status 409
Received status 201
Exchange PUT http://sut/ehr/3f2a -&gt; 201   (recording entry 2)
Whose    the server: a failed row counts against the claimed capability
         the cited text has a known spec gap: upstream report #42</failure>
    </testcase>
  </testsuite>
  <testsuite name="ehr/etag" tests="1" failures="0" errors="0" skipped="0">
